Language English

Book Crypt Ordered No Keep Looped
	Page ExploreViaChapel
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreCryptViaChapel
		No Text
		
		exploredCryptViaChapel = true
		exploredCryptViaDungeonCave = false
		Goto PlaceCrypt
	End Page ExploreViaChapel
	
	Page ExploreViaDungeonCave
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreCryptViaDungeonCave
		No Text
		
		exploredCryptViaDungeonCave = true
		exploredCryptViaChapel = false
		Goto PlaceCrypt
	End Page
	
	Page PlaceCrypt
		Not Visible
		
		Prolog "The cave continues into the darkness."
		Button "Reveal"
		
		Add TileCrypt
		Remove TokenExploreCryptViaDungeonCave
		Remove TokenSearchCryptViaChapel
		
		Text """
			You walk forward a bit and realize the other part of the cave
			is a crypt containing above-ground stone caskets. The air is
			different, even from the cave you have been in.
			
			Place the {c:TileCrypt} tile and discard this Sight token.
		"""
		
		If exploredCryptViaChapel Then Text """
			You peer into the dark space but cannot see much, so you step
			through the doorway. You eyes adjust quickly to the light.
			
			Place the {c:TileCrypt} tile, discard this Search and any
			Sight tokens leading to the explored area, then move 1 space into
			the explored area.
		"""
		
		Goto PlaceSearchPendant
	End Page PlaceCrypt
	
	Page PlaceSearchPendant
		Not Visible
		Add TokenSearchCryptPendant!
		
		Text """
			One of the stone caskets is open. You aren't sure you want to look
			inside. Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Goto PlaceSearchPeter
	End Page PlaceSearchPendant
	
	Page PlaceSearchPeter
		Not Visible
		
		Add TokenSearchCryptPeter!
		Text """
			The stone casket on the end looks much newer than the others. Place
			a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		If Not exploredDungeonCave Then Goto PlaceExploreDungeonCaveViaCrypt
		If Not exploredCryptViaChapel Then Goto PlaceExploreChapelViaCrypt
		Exit
	End Page PlaceSearchPeter

	Page PlaceExploreChapelViaCrypt
		Not Visible
		
		Add TokenSearchChapelViaCrypt!
		
		Text """
			Something about the wall seems... off. Place a Search token
			as indicated.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page PlaceExploreChapelViaCrypt
	
	Page PlaceExploreDungeonCaveViaCrypt
		Not Visible
		
		Add TokenExploreDungeonCaveViaCrypt!
		Text """
			The back of crypt is too dark to see from here. Place a Sight
			token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page PlaceExploreDungeonCaveViaCrypt
	
	Page SearchChapelViaCrypt
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchChapelViaCrypt
		
		Prolog """
			The wall in front of you is smooth rock. But is that a cut?
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Text """
			You walk up to the wall and put your hands on it, moving around
			until you see it:  a razor-thin, rectangular cut into the rock. The
			cut is about the size of the doors inside the house. Maybe
			this is a door too?
			
			A lot of time passes before you give up looking for a way
			to open it. Your turn ends immediately and you skip your next turn.
			
			Discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenSearchChapelViaCrypt
		Exit
	End Page SearchChapelViaCrypt
	
	Page SearchPendant
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchCryptPendant
		
		Prolog """
			You walk over to the open stone casket. You wonder what might have
			been interred with the body. And whether there is anything left
			after whatever descecration left the casket open.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenSearchCryptPendant
		
		Text QItemElderSignPendant """
			Mixed in with the bones, tattered clothing, and cobwebs are several
			pieces of junk jewelry, tarnished and of no value. But there is one
			piece that looks like it might be worth something. Gain the
			{c:QItemElderSignPendant} Common Item, then discard this Search
			token.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page SearchPendant
	
	Page SearchPeter
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchCryptPeter
		
		Prolog """
			A brass plate on top of the stone casket looks like it has the name
			of the person inside. The letters dance and swim, much like the text
			in the {c:QItemDvm}.
			
			Only {c:EventChosenInvestigator} can read the inscription.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Text """
			When you lean over to read it, the letters coalesce into the name
			and dates of the person inside.
			
			Here lies Peter Smythe\n
			Born 12 May, 1885 -- Died 31 October, 1915

			It seems your father didn't leave, he died after stopping the ritual
			10 years ago, probably killed by your uncle. You cannot remember
			him, but thinking about him lying dead three feet away makes your
			chest hurt.
			
			Discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		peterIsDead = true
		Remove TokenSearchCryptPeter
		Exit
	End Page SearchPeter
End Book Crypt